---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Rewards Platform · Rodion Ostrovskii"
  description="Case study: a full-stack rewards platform with an Angular frontend, a Spring Boot REST API, PostgreSQL and CI/CD in GitHub Actions."
  active="projects"
>
  <main class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="project-details">
        <h1 class="title-1">Rewards Platform</h1>
  
        <!-- Swap for a screenshot when you have one: <img src="/img/rewards-big.jpg" alt="Rewards catalog screen"> -->
        <div class="project-details__cover" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="cover-art"><b>Points → Rewards</b><span>Angular · Spring Boot · PostgreSQL</span></div>
        </div>
  
        <div class="project-details__desc">
          <p>Skills: Angular, Spring Boot, PostgreSQL, REST API, Docker, GitHub Actions CI</p>
        </div>
  
        <div class="project-details__actions">
          <a href="https://github.com/ostrovsrr/rewards-program" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="btn-outline"><img src="/img/github-black.svg" alt="">GitHub repo</a>
        </div>
  
        <div class="case">
          <h2 class="title-2">What it does</h2>
          <p>A loyalty rewards app. Members check their points balance and activity history, browse a catalog of partner rewards (travel, gift cards, merchandise and statement credits) and redeem points for them.</p>
  
          <h2 class="title-2">How it's built</h2>
          <ul class="bullets">
            <li><strong>REST API in Spring Boot</strong> for users, the rewards catalog and redemptions, consumed by the Angular frontend.</li>
            <li><strong>Redemptions that can't double-spend.</strong> Each redemption runs in one transaction: the member's row is locked, the balance is checked and debited, and the activity and redemption records are written together. The database also rejects a negative balance.</li>
            <li><strong>Data access with JPA and Hibernate</strong>, with the schema and seed catalog managed as Flyway migrations.</li>
            <li><strong>Tested</strong> with unit and integration tests (Karma and Jasmine on the frontend).</li>
            <li><strong>PostgreSQL in Docker Compose</strong>, GitHub Actions CI for the frontend, and a feature-branch workflow.</li>
          </ul>
  
          <p class="next-link"><a href="/floor-is-lava">Next project: Floor is Lava →</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
